# SignalScope AI — Intelligent Telemetry Analytics Platform

**Turn telemetry events into evidence-backed engineering decisions.**

SignalScope AI is an end-to-end research prototype that generates synthetic software-service telemetry, stores it in DuckDB and Parquet, detects anomalous behavior, compares software releases, and answers a limited set of natural-language analytics questions using computed evidence.

The default analyst is deterministic and requires no LLM key. This is intentional: analytics code computes the findings, and the explanation layer should not invent measurements. An optional LLM can be added later behind a structured, evidence-validation layer.

## Capabilities

- Simulates 30 days of hourly telemetry across 50 services and 3 regions.
- Injects a labelled regression affecting three services in `us-east`.
- Validates and ingests telemetry through FastAPI/Pydantic.
- Stores records in DuckDB and exports Parquet.
- Detects unusual latency, error-rate, CPU, memory, and queue-depth behavior using robust baseline thresholds.
- Compares release metrics with absolute/relative changes and sample counts.
- Answers supported questions about regressions, anomalies, latency, and summaries.
- Provides a Streamlit/Plotly dashboard, API docs, evaluation metrics, and tests.
- Includes Docker packaging for the API.

## Architecture

```text
Synthetic telemetry -> FastAPI/Pydantic -> DuckDB -> Parquet export
                                      |
                     +----------------+----------------+
                     |                |                |
               Anomaly detection  Release analysis  Evidence-grounded Q&A
                     |                |                |
                     +----------------+----------------+
                                      |
                            FastAPI + Streamlit
                                      |
                         Reproducible evaluation/tests
```

